The function is already a single pointer-chase load with no arithmetic to remove, so I kept the exact same access but hoisted the array base into a local to give the compiler a clean single dependent load and avoid any redundant re-evaluation of the member chain.

```cpp
FIT_BOOL Field::GetIsAccumulated() const
{
    const Profile::Field* fields = profile->fields;
    return fields[profileIndex].isAccumulated;
}
```